concept permanent_note {
  name     = "Permanent Note"
  summary  = "A note refined for keeps: one idea, in your own words, self-contained and linked — the standard every wskill unit is held to."
  related  = [atomic_note, zettelkasten, selfcontained]
  body {
    p <<BODY
      A permanent note is one that is written to last. It states a single idea fully and in
      your own words, stands on its own without needing the source it came from, and is linked
      into the rest of the notes so it can be found again. Producing one takes deliberate work:
      you decide what the idea really is, phrase it cleanly, and connect it to what you already
      have.
    BODY

    p <<BODY
      Every unit in a wskill is a permanent note. A concept, entity, fact or process is held to
      exactly this standard — atomic, self-contained, and cross-referenced through `related` —
      because the unit is the durable record the templates project. A rough first draft is the
      raw input; the permanent note is what the wskill actually stores.
    BODY
  }
}
